CORE gcc-only
main.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion .*isless.*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ assertion .*isunordered.*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ assertion __builtin_isless\(a, l\): SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Goto conversion called __CPROVER_isless{f,d} and friends, which were not
declared ("identifier __CPROVER_islessd was not found"), and rejected a
long double argument.  The macros are now the relations they denote.
